            <ArticleTitle>A novel concept in endovascular stenting for the treatment of old severely degenerated saphenous vein graft in the urgent setting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>957-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccd.22323</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a critically ill-patient admitted for NSTEMI with acute pulmonary congestion, showing at urgent cardiac catheterization a severely diseased saphenous vein graft as the culprit vessel, with huge atherothrombotic burden. The graft was successfully revascularized by the implantation of 4 M-Guard stent (for proximal to distal) creating a full metal jacket. The M-Guard technology consists on a stainless steel platform wrapped by a micron-level polymer net, that seamlessly expands when the stent is deployed, providing protection from embolic showers.</AbstractText>
